fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
# The `/effort ` inline column (fx 04a5e3af, E6; P5-EF2): the current model's
# levels under the argument of an `/effort ` line, no key-help row, the
# status line previewing the marked level, its filter, Tab filling
# `/effort <level>`, and Enter applying the level.
#
# First the research run's column block, from the same state (the level in
# use is `default`): `level-upper` (`/effort HIGH` applied as `high`, through
# the column's Enter, whose filter ignores case:
# `app_input_runtime.zig:1421@481104fd` -> `submitEffortPicker`,
# `input_completion_runtime.zig:1476`), then `col-space` ... `col-enter`.
#
# Then, with `low` in use, what that block cannot tell apart: a Space opens
# the column on its first row and Tab on the level in use
# (`openCurrentEffortPicker`, `:1314-1328`); a space typed in the column is
# its own and goes nowhere; Enter takes the marked row of a filter that
# matches more than one; Escape puts the column away and the line stays, so
# Enter runs the bare command; and a prefix applies the level it matches.
models p5-effort-fork-models.json
seed p5-effort-fork-seed-astra.json
nomodel
wait 3
snap launch
paste /effort HIGH
wait 0.4
key Enter
wait 1
snap level-upper
paste /effort default
wait 0.4
key Enter
wait 1
snap level-default
type /effort
key Space
wait 0.8
snap col-space
key Down
wait 0.4
snap col-down
type zz
wait 0.4
snap col-nomatch
key C-u
wait 0.3
type /effort
key Tab
wait 0.8
snap col-tab
key Down
wait 0.3
key Tab
wait 0.5
snap col-fill
key Enter
wait 1
snap col-enter
home after-col
type /effort
key Space
wait 0.8
snap space-first
key C-u
wait 0.3
type /effort
key Tab
wait 0.8
snap tab-current
type hi
key Space
wait 0.5
snap typed-space
key Down
wait 0.4
snap typed-down
key Enter
wait 1
snap typed-enter
home after-typed
type /effort
key Tab
wait 0.8
key Escape
wait 0.5
snap col-esc
key Enter
wait 1
snap esc-enter
key Escape
wait 0.5
paste /effort med
wait 0.4
key Enter
wait 1
snap level-prefix
home end
